#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens is a software supply-chain security tool, so the security of the "
"tool itself matters too. If you find a vulnerability, please report it "
"responsibly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: SECURITY.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Supported versions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Security fixes are provided for the latest release. The "
"`ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest` Docker image tag (legacy alias: "
"`sbom-scanner:latest`) reflects the latest security patches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Version | Supported |\n"
"|---------|-----------|\n"
"| Latest release (`:latest`) | ✅ |\n"
"| Older versions | ❌ |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are on an older version, please upgrade to the latest release first "
"and check whether the issue still reproduces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: SECURITY.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reporting a vulnerability"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please do **not** open a public issue. Report privately through one of the "
"two channels below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: SECURITY.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. GitHub Private Vulnerability Reporting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this repository's **Security** tab, click **Report a vulnerability** to "
"submit a private advisory draft. It is visible only to maintainers, and the "
"fix and disclosure schedule can be coordinated in the same place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: SECURITY.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You may also email "
"[opensource@sktelecom.com](mailto:opensource@sktelecom.com)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: SECURITY.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What to include"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "The type of vulnerability and its impact"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "The affected file path or code location"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Reproduction steps or a proof of concept (PoC)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "If possible, the affected version and environment (OS, Docker version)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: SECURITY.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Process"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When we receive a report, we respond along the following lines. This is a "
"volunteer-based project, so the timelines below are targets and may vary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid "Acknowledge receipt within 3 business days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Review, determine whether it is a vulnerability and its severity, and inform "
"the reporter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If a fix is needed, prepare a patch and coordinate the disclosure timing "
"with the reporter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: SECURITY.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Once the fix is released, publish the security advisory and, if desired, "
"credit the reporter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: SECURITY.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Private reports are not shared externally until the fix and coordination are "
"complete."
msgstr ""

