#. type: Title #
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Third-Party Licenses"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> **한국어**: [THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.ko.md](THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.ko.md)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens (Apache-2.0) keeps its own code in shell scripts and bundles several "
"open-source tools into its Docker images to generate and analyze SBOMs. This "
"document is the license inventory for the bundled tools and the distribution "
"obligations that come with them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compliance summary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The BomLens shell scripts invoke the bundled tools as separate processes "
"(exec) and do not modify their sources. The copyleft of GPL and AGPL tools "
"therefore does not propagate to the Apache-2.0 code of BomLens (per the FSF "
"reading: pipes, CLI calls, and exec make separate programs; bundling in a "
"container is mere aggregation)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The tool binaries are still redistributed inside the images, so the license "
"texts and, for GPL tools, a path to the corresponding source are "
"provided. The SPDX license texts (Apache-2.0, MIT, GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, and "
"others) ship inside the images at `/usr/local/lib/sbom/licenses/`, and each "
"tool's source is available from the Source URL in the tables below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"BomLens ships its own terms with every distribution. In the images they are "
"at `/usr/local/lib/sbom/notices/`, holding `LICENSE`, `NOTICE`, and this "
"document; in the release bundles they sit at the top of the extracted tree; "
"in the desktop installer they are in the app's resources folder. Passing "
"those files along when you redistribute an image or a bundle is what "
"Apache-2.0 §4 asks for."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"No AGPL-licensed tool is included. Running the web UI (`--ui`) therefore "
"does not trigger the AGPL §13 network clause."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The GPL-licensed analysis tools live only in a separate opt-in image "
"(`bomlens-firmware`). The tools installed into the base image (`bomlens`) "
"and into the other opt-in images (`bomlens-aibom`, `bomlens-deep-cve`) are "
"permissive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Every image, the base one included, is built on `python:3.12-slim` and "
"therefore also contains Debian system packages under the GPL, the LGPL and "
"other licenses. That is inherent to any Linux base image; there is no "
"GPL-free one. See [Debian packages in every "
"image](#debian-packages-in-every-image) below for what this means and where "
"the source is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Base image — `ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens` (BomLens tools; see also the Debian "
"base below)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool | Purpose | License (SPDX) | Source |\n"
"|------|---------|----------------|--------|\n"
"| cdxgen (official language images) | SBOM generation from source | "
"Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/CycloneDX/cdxgen |\n"
"| syft | SBOM for images, binaries, and directories | Apache-2.0 | "
"https://github.com/anchore/syft |\n"
"| Trivy | Vulnerability scanning | Apache-2.0 | "
"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy |\n"
"| trivy-db | Vulnerability database | Apache-2.0 | "
"https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy-db |\n"
"| cosign | SBOM signing | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/sigstore/cosign "
"|\n"
"| scancode-toolkit | Detailed license detection. Build-time opt-in "
"(`SBOM_DEEP_LICENSE=true`); **not present in the published images**, which "
"are built with the default `false` | Apache-2.0 (parts of the dataset "
"CC-BY-4.0 and others) | https://github.com/aboutcode-org/scancode-toolkit "
"|\n"
"| scanoss (scanoss.py) | Vendored open-source identification (bundled by "
"default; disable with `SBOM_SCANOSS=false`) | MIT (the bundled "
"`osadl-copyleft.json` dataset is CC-BY-4.0) | "
"https://github.com/scanoss/scanoss.py |\n"
"| owasp-aibom-generator | AI model SBOM generation (opt-in `SBOM_AIBOM`, "
"separate image `bomlens-aibom`; calls the HuggingFace API) | Apache-2.0 | "
"https://github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/aibom-generator |\n"
"| picklescan | Pickle analysis for scanned AI model files — whether loading "
"the weights would run code (always installed; pure Python, no network) | MIT "
"| https://github.com/mmaitre314/picklescan |\n"
"| jq | SBOM post-processing helper | MIT (some components BSD, ICU, or "
"Lucent) | https://github.com/jqlang/jq |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Data: NVD, the vulnerability source, is public domain and requires "
"attribution to \"NIST/NVD\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bundled data snapshots"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Two datasets are fetched once at image-build time and shipped inside the "
"base image so the offline checks that read them need no network access at "
"scan time. The build scripts that fetch them are deleted from the image "
"afterwards, so the attribution is recorded here instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Data | Bundled at | Source | License |\n"
"|------|-----------|--------|---------|\n"
"| End-of-life dates | `/usr/local/lib/sbom/eol-data.json`, "
"`eol-purl-map.json` | [endoflife.date](https://endoflife.date), read from "
"its public API | MIT |\n"
"| Malicious package advisories | `/usr/local/lib/sbom/malicious-index.json` "
"| OSV bulk archives (`osv-vulnerabilities.storage.googleapis.com`). The "
"`MAL-` records they carry are published by the OpenSSF Package Analysis "
"project, "
"[ossf/malicious-packages](https://github.com/ossf/malicious-packages) | "
"Apache-2.0 (upstream advisory repository) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Neither dataset is reproduced whole. Each is reduced to what the check "
"actually reads — a product's end-of-life dates, or a PURL keyed to its "
"advisory id — and the snapshot date travels with it, both in the bundled "
"file and on every component the check flags (`bomlens:eol:source`, "
"`bomlens:malicious:source`). Neither project endorses or certifies BomLens, "
"and the bundled data is provided as is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:45
