#. type: Title ##
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:169
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Android SDK image — built by you, not published"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:172
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"cdxgen publishes no Android-SDK-bearing image and marks Android as having no "
"transitive support, so an Android project cannot be delegated to "
"it. `docker/android/Dockerfile` adds an Android SDK platform on top of "
"cdxgen's java image, one image per `compileSdk`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:174
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**We do not publish this image.** The Android SDK is not open source, and "
"its terms permit copying only for backup and bar redistribution except where "
"a third-party licence requires otherwise "
"([§3.4](https://developer.android.com/studio/terms); §3.5 limits that "
"exception to the SDK's open-source components). Putting the image in a "
"public registry would hand the SDK to everyone who pulls it, which is what "
"that clause names. So each user builds it once and accepts Google's terms "
"directly, the same as installing Android Studio:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docker build --build-arg ANDROID_API=35 -t bomlens-android-sdk35 "
"docker/android\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:180
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`scan-sbom.sh` detects the project's `compileSdk` and prints this command "
"when the matching image is missing. `ANDROID_IMAGE_PREFIX` points it at an "
"image built elsewhere — including the "
"`ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-android-sdk<API>` images published up to v1.9.0, "
"before this was decided. Those are left in place so scans on released "
"versions keep working; nothing new is pushed to them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:182
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The image holds no BomLens code, so it is not covered by our Apache-2.0 "
"grant. What it contains:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:187
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Component | Source | Terms |\n"
"|-----------|--------|-------|\n"
"| cdxgen java image (`cdxgen-temurin-java21`, digest-pinned) | "
"https://github.com/CycloneDX/cdxgen | Apache-2.0 |\n"
"| Android SDK command-line tools, platform-tools, `platforms;android-<API>`, "
"`build-tools;<API>.0.0` | Installed by `sdkmanager` from "
"https://dl.google.com/android/repository/ | Android Software Development Kit "
"License Agreement, https://developer.android.com/studio/terms |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:189
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The SDK terms also grant only a non-sublicensable licence to use the SDK for "
"developing Android applications (§3.1), which is a further reason the image "
"cannot be handed on: we have nothing to sublicense."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:191
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Each SDK component carries its own `NOTICE.txt` inside the image (under "
"`/opt/android-sdk/`), which is where the third-party notices for the SDK's "
"own contents live. The `/opt/android-sdk/licenses/` files are acceptance "
"markers written by `sdkmanager`, not licence texts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:192
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Desktop installer — Electron and Chromium"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md:195
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
